## Known environment gotchas (hit multiple times today — worth having
handy)

- **`docker exec -it` + piped heredoc fails**: "cannot attach stdin to a
  TTY-enabled container because stdin is not a terminal." Fix: drop `-t`,
  use `-i` only, for any non-interactive command receiving piped input
  (heredocs, loops).
- **Host-side file permissions**: `wp-content` is owned by
  `www-data`/`root` inside the container. Direct `mkdir`/`touch`/vim edits
  from the host shell can fail with `Permission denied`, or succeed but
  leave files unwritable later (as happened with `custom.css` this
  session). Workarounds used today: create/edit via `docker exec ...
  bash -c "cat > ..." << 'EOF'`, or `sudo chown simon:simon <file>` once,
  after which normal host-side vim editing works.
- **Slug vs. title vs. typed URL mismatches**: caused real confusion
  twice today (`hello-world` vs `helloworld`, page 92's stale "Coming
  soon" title). WordPress matches purely by slug for template hierarchy
  and URL routing — title is cosmetic and can drift independently. Worth
  checking `wp post list` slugs directly rather than trusting a typed URL
  or a page title when something seems "stuck."
- **`while read` loops piping into `docker exec -it`**: same TTY problem
  as heredocs — every iteration fails identically. Use `-i` inside the
  loop body.

